  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An elliptical loop having resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, of semi major axis&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> , and semi minor axis&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> &nbsp;is placed in a magnetic field as shown in the figure. If the loop is rotated about the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis with angular frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>, the average power loss in the loop due to Joule heating is :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c5b72a4a-b084-4e91-889f-2dc30d07c828-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 136px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
